{
  "slug": "euler-totient-oq-02",
  "title": "Multiplicative Property of Euler Totient Function",
  "phase": "NEW",
  "status": "active",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "fast",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\gcd(m,n)=1\\Rightarrow \\varphi(mn)=\\varphi(m)\\varphi(n),\\quad \\varphi(p^k)=p^k-p^{k-1}\\text{ for prime }p\\text{ and }k>0.",
    "plain": "Backfill the Euler totient multiplicativity entry around the CRT-based product formula, prime-power computation, and the identification of `Nat.totient n` with the unit group of `ZMod n`.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Totient multiplicativity is the basic structural theorem behind many elementary number-theory computations.",
      "Prime-power formulas plus coprime multiplicativity determine the totient function from factorizations.",
      "The Lean proofs connect the arithmetic statement to finite unit groups and the Chinese remainder theorem."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "`totient_mul_coprime` and `totient_mul_of_gcd_eq_one` prove multiplicativity under coprimality.",
      "`totient_prime_pow` proves the prime-power formula.",
      "`totient_eq_card_units` identifies the totient with the cardinality of `(ZMod n)^*`.",
      "`totient_mul_crt_explanation` records the CRT explanation for the multiplicative formula, and `euler_totient` supplies the Euler-theorem parent result."
    ],
